---
description: Keep argsbarg examples in sync when changing builtins or schemagen conventions
globs: "src/builtins/**/*,src/capabilities.ts,src/config/**/*,src/docs/**/*,src/install/**/*,src/mcp/**/*,docs/output-schema.md,docs/config-schema.md"
alwaysApply: false
---

When changing argsbarg **builtins**, **capabilities**, or **schemagen documentation**:

1. Update **`examples/full-example/`** so it still enables every capability (`completion`, `version`, `configure`, `docs`, `mcp`).
2. Run **`just check-full-example`** from the argsbarg repo root (schemagen + schema git diff + `create --check`).
3. Run **`just test`** — includes `src/cli-tool/full-example-capabilities.test.ts`.

**Copy template:** `examples/full-example/` — all builtins, schemagen, Homebrew justfile, `outputSchema`, `from "argsbarg"`.

Do not duplicate framework docs here — see `docs/cli-program.md` and shipped `cli-program.mdc`.
